<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Statutes of Lithuania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1529">1529</a>–<a href="/years/1588">1588</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Lithuanian Statutes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Statutes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> were three law codes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>, issued in 1529, 1566 and 1588 and written in Ruthenian. They codified the rights of the nobility, courts and procedure and were among the most advanced legal codes of their time. The third statute remained in force in parts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> until 1840.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/statutes-of-lithuania.jpg" alt="Statutes of Lithuania" width="320" height="354" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_Grand_Duchy_of_Lithuania_from_the_Statute_(1614).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
